## 6. Part 4: 7-Stage Architecture Realization & User-Authorized Bend Authority

### A. Root Cause: Why Did Opening a Raw 45° DXF Show "19 Openings"?
When opening a raw blank (`45_deg_bend_100x100.dxf`), the file has $0$ bend lines.
The previous code immediately attempted to fold the document and discover 3D ports. Folding a sheet with $0$ bends yields $1$ flat polygon (unfolded). The 3D opening detector looks for edges of the base floor with no bend lines attached. Because there were $0$ bends anywhere on the workpiece, **all 19 outer boundary edges** had no bend lines attached, so the algorithm falsely reported $19$ channel openings and triggered the ambiguity resolver dialog before authoring had even begun!

### B. Foundational Axiom
> *"A flat DXF has no physical ports. Ports are semantic physical openings of the folded part. Therefore, CMS port discovery is strictly prohibited until the user-authorized bend structure has produced a valid folded 3D topology."*

### C. The 7-Stage Authoring Pipeline
```
Stage 1: Product Intent
   │  Catalog contract loaded (e.g. 45° Bend expects 2 ports, 3 structural bends, 2 flanges)
   ▼
Stage 2: Bend Structure (User-Authorized)
   │  Analyze flat blank ➔ Suggest candidate bend & flange lines
   │  PAUSE: Render dashed cyan/teal suggestions with terminal dots & badges on 2D canvas
   │  User clicks [Use Suggested Bends] or draws manually (B)
   ▼
Stage 3: 3D Channel Fold
   │  Forward kinematics folds upright channel (0° flat ➔ 90° upright)
   │  HARD GUARD: Prohibit 3D port discovery if folded mesh has <= 1 face
   ▼
Stage 4: Physical Ports
   │  Scan terminal open loops of the 3D channel
   │  Automatic correlation with contract (PORT_1, PORT_2 matched automatically without ambiguity)
   ▼
Stage 5: Feature Protection
   │  Lock rigid 8×12mm coupler slots to sidewalls as scale invariants
   ▼
Stage 6: Smart Scaling
   │  Establish topological constraints between ports, sidewalls, and flanges
   ▼
Stage 7: Template Complete
   │  Verified CMS template ready for parametric scaling and catalog storage
```

### D. Key Implementation Details
1. **User Authority**:
   - The system never silently converts candidate lines into real bends.
   - UI button explicitly states: `[Use Suggested Bends]`, signifying: *"Use these highlighted lines as my bend definitions"*.
2. **Contract-Driven Bend Validation**:
   - `document.bends.isNotEmpty` is no longer blindly trusted. Bends are validated against `contract.expectedStructuralBends`.
   - If insufficient or uncertain, the controller transitions to `CmsUxPhase.confirmingBends`.
3. **2D Canvas Overlay Enhancements**:
   - [cms_2d_overlay_painter.dart](file:///d:/FlutterProjects/trufold_studio/lib/sheet_metal_studio/views/widgets/guided_cms/cms_2d_overlay_painter.dart) renders dashed lines with terminal anchor dots, outer halos, and midpoint badges (`FLANGE 90° UP`, `BEND 90° UP`) during Stage 2 suggestions.
4. **Hard Guards**:
   - [cms_guided_ux_controller.dart](file:///d:/FlutterProjects/trufold_studio/lib/sheet_metal_studio/engine/cms/cms_guided_ux_controller.dart) enforces that if `foldResult.polygons.length <= 1`, execution halts with `CmsUxPhase.error`, completely preventing false opening scans on flat blanks.

