## 7. Part 5: Phase 1 Polish — Accurate 3D Anchors, Perimeter Borders & Fitting Inspector Modernization

Based on interactive testing and user feedback:

### A. Pegged 3D Opening Mouth Anchors (Eliminating the Floating Bug)
- **Problem**: Previously, [CmsOpeningPlaneAnalyzer](file:///d:/FlutterProjects/trufold_studio/lib/sheet_metal_studio/engine/cms/cms_opening_plane_analyzer.dart) added $+H/2$ blindly to the floor face $Z$ level ($100.0\text{ mm}$), causing port callouts to float at $Z = 162.1\text{ mm}$ high up in empty space above inverted channels.
- **Solution**:
  1. Detects actual sidewall vertex $Z$ levels from the folded mesh (finding true $lipZ = 0.5\text{ mm}$ for inverted $100\text{ mm}$ standing channel models).
  2. Computes the 4 exact 3D corners of the channel opening mouth:
     - Floor threshold corners: $P1, P2$
     - Top lip corners: $P3 = (P1.x, P1.y, lipZ)$, $P4 = (P2.x, P2.y, lipZ)$
  3. Calculates the mouth centroid at $((P1+P2)/2, (P1.z+lipZ)/2) \approx Z = 50.3\text{ mm}$.
  4. Anchors the callout badge directly to the mouth top-rim edge $((P1+P2)/2, lipZ)$ with a pinned 3D leader peg:
     - Badge displays anchored above the mouth with a vertical leader line connecting directly to an anchor dot on the rim.

### B. High-Visibility 3D Aperture Fill & Glowing Perimeter Highlight Loop
- **File**: [viewport_3d_widget.dart](file:///d:/FlutterProjects/trufold_studio/lib/sheet_metal_studio/views/widgets/viewport_3d_widget.dart)
